From e5f19151db20aa5e3856f68efb3cd4aa70313743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] video-driver: iris33: size H.264/HEVC COMV for the
 worst DPB

Until the first input settings change, the H.264/HEVC COMV (collocated
motion vector) buffer is sized for the default output min count (4).
When capture is streamed on before the first sequence header is
parsed, the capture START can reach the firmware while it parses that
header. The firmware then raises the settings change and, without
waiting for the host, fails the session:

  h264DecCalcBufReq(1912): num of col buffer not enough. host 4 < fw 6
  Session Error: HFI_ERROR_FATAL - vfw_h264_main.c:1916

An HFI trace has the capture START 61 us before the settings change
and the fatal 386 us after it, nothing sent by the host in between.
FFmpeg streams capture on early and failed 3 of 160 sessions on a
256x144 H.264 clip; a client that streams capture on 0-1500 us after
the first bitstream buffer failed 9 of 215 H.264/HEVC sessions.

Until the firmware has reported its count, size COMV for the largest
DPB H.264 and HEVC allow, 16 pictures plus the current one: 0 of 215
then fail. At 4096x2176 that is 74.5 MiB for H.264 and 144.5 MiB for
HEVC instead of 17.5 and 34 MiB, released by the previous patch when
the client completes the reconfig. Thumbnail sessions are unchanged.

Fixes: 3d9c6f17f9fa ("video: driver: Add support for lanai/iris3.3 platform")
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [qualcomm-linux/video-driver]
---
 driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_buffer_iris33.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_buffer_iris33.c b/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_buffer_iris33.c
index b92e979f..40d48257 100644
--- a/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_buffer_iris33.c
+++ b/driver/variant/iris33/src/msm_vidc_buffer_iris33.c
@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@ static u32 msm_vidc_decoder_bin_size_iris33(struct msm_vidc_inst *inst)
 	return size;
 }
 
+/* H.264 A.3.1 and HEVC A.4.2 cap the DPB at 16 pictures */
+#define H26X_MAX_DPB_FRAMES 16
+
 static u32 msm_vidc_decoder_comv_size_iris33(struct msm_vidc_inst *inst)
 {
 	u32 size = 0;
@@ -81,6 +84,16 @@ static u32 msm_vidc_decoder_comv_size_iris33(struct msm_vidc_inst *inst)
 		else
 			num_comv = inst->fw_min_count ?
 				inst->fw_min_count + 7 : inst->buffers.output.min_count + 7;
+	} else if (!inst->fw_min_count && !is_thumbnail_session(inst) &&
+		   (inst->codec == MSM_VIDC_H264 || inst->codec == MSM_VIDC_HEVC)) {
+		/*
+		 * A capture START that reaches the firmware while it parses the
+		 * first sequence header makes it check COMV against the stream
+		 * right after the settings change and fail the session when
+		 * short. Cover the largest DPB plus the current picture until
+		 * the firmware reports its count.
+		 */
+		num_comv = H26X_MAX_DPB_FRAMES + 1;
 	} else {
 		num_comv = inst->buffers.output.min_count;
 	}
